extends RefCounted
## Tool swings. Durations and contact frames match ActionFrames.DURATIONS and
## ActionFrames.contact_ratio (hits land on frame 4 of 8 for every tool), so
## gameplay timing is unchanged while the motion gets anticipation, a clear
## impact frame and follow-through.
##
## Shared beat for every swing (8 frames):
##   0     lift off the carry pose (idle/walk hold the tool the same way)
##   1-2   anticipation: cock the tool back/up, body rises; 2 ~holds 1
##   3     the fast smear frame
##   4     IMPACT: body drops a pixel, head squashes into the collar, the front
##         foot plants, the off hand swings the other way
##   5     hold the hit (reads as weight / hit-stop)
##   6-7   settle back towards the carry pose so locomotion picks up cleanly
##
## Front view: windups raise the tool high on the main-hand side with the arm
## tucked behind the head ("down_arms_behind"), so the tool is clearly beside
## or above the helmet and no arm ever crosses the face. The chibi arms are
## ~5.6 px long, so two-handed grips only meet at the chest centre: two-handed
## tools raise one-handed and the off hand joins on the downswing.
## Back view: the raised tool is drawn over the head ("up_arms_front"); at the
## hit it is swung away from the camera and hidden by the body.
## Field reference: res://Forest/keeper/KeeperMotion.gd

